  "Detailed Rules IDB-31 'Which MVP defs carry an emits' (463); Visual/Audio lantern row; AC-26; Interactions rows for Emitter State (950) and Lighting: [main review, confirmed by creative-director] The lantern contract conflicts across documents. Item DB line 463 gives `emits` to `mod_lamp`, `mod_reactor_cell`, `mod_coolant_pump` and `cons_glowstick` only, and says 'No other def carries one'. Derelict Authoring DA-24 (:422) counts 8 world lanterns, `scr_main`, `scr_a` and `scr_b` among them, and says 'the failed scrubber never lights'. Boarding builds its scr_a witness on a scrubber lantern (:234, :697 EC-BS-17, :1028, :1536 AC-BS-48, :1669). Emitter State EM-14 (:220) only gives an example list, '(a pump, a reactor)'. It does not restrict the kinds. As the roster stands, E1 can create only 5 lanterns. That makes the 8-lantern budget, the Lighting lantern input and the Boarding falsifier beat impossible to implement. I checked the sibling GDDs and none of them resolves this. FIX: [creative-director ruling, under delegated G6] The scrubbers get a lantern. The other choice, conforming DA-24 and Boarding to an unlit scrubber, is rejected. Pillar 1 says the world never lies: an air scrubber is the machine the crew most needs to read at a glance, and the scr_a dark-lantern beat is the clearest falsifier witness in the MVP. Add `emits {LANTERN, base_pm [PH], LANTERN_O2}` with the default `lantern_on_states` {0 OK, 1 DEGRADED} to `mod_scrubber` in IDB-31 line 463. Make the same change in the Visual/Audio table, and in AC-26, which then lists five defs. Bring the Emitter State and Lighting Interactions rows into line. Ask the Emitter State writer to restate EM-14 as 'the kinds whose def carries `emits`'. Re-verify the count against DA-24 (world 8 of 20) and the registry entry mvp_fixture_counts. LANTERN_LIGHTS_MAX is 8 in view, so check the worst-case view on the home ship."
